   "mark": "1",
   "text": "In fact the tautological bundle often is not well-defined as a vector bundle.It is well-defined as a projective bundle, and the “determinant” det E is also well-defined, but the determinant might have no n-th root and correspondingly c1(det E) ∈H2(XD, Z) may not be divisible by n. Since we are dealing with the cohomology with complex coefficients, this does not create a problem and all the Chern classes are still well-defined.",
